---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Content as Essay } from '../content/corpus/metadata_independence_essay_v0_2.md';
import { Content as Seam } from '../content/corpus/silent_seam_companion_v1_0.md';
import TermChipStrip from '../components/TermChipStrip.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Why — datumwise">
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Why</p>
  </div>
  {/* STANDING, NOT A REWRITE (positioning repair §4, 2026-08-27) — see thesis.astro for the ruling.
      Both essays below are frozen corpus editions; the bytes are not edited. "The semantic layer was
      only ever half the answer. The other half now exists." is the launch-era argument as published,
      and it stays. What was missing was the date on it. */}
  <p class="standing wayfinding">
    <span class="standing-mark mono">editions</span>
    <span><em>Metadata Independence</em> (draft v0.2) and <em>The Silent Seam</em> (v1.0, June 2026),
    reproduced here as written. Both are dated arguments, not current statements of what datumwise or
    Columna is; for that, see <a href="/about">About</a> and <a href="/columna">Columna</a>.</span>
  </p>
  <article class="prose">
    <Essay />
    <hr />
    <p class="seam-note">The Silent Seam below was published against the Atlas's v1.0 count of sixty-six modes; the Atlas has since added one — the sixty-seven cited elsewhere on this site.</p>
    <Seam />
  </article>
  <p class="further-reading">Further reading: how this positions against semantic layers, modeling languages, and text-to-SQL — <a href="/ladder">The Ladder</a>.</p>
  <TermChipStrip />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .standing { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; align-items: baseline; margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .standing-mark { font-size: 0.68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--ink-faint); white-space: nowrap; }
  .standing a { color: var(--ink); }

  .further-reading { width: min(100% - 3rem, 46rem); margin: 2rem auto 0; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft, #555); }
  /* editorial reconciliation note (the site's voice) — the reproduced Seam essay is byte-identical */
  .seam-note { width: min(100% - 3rem, 46rem); margin: 0 auto 1.5rem; font-size: 0.86rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-soft, #666); }
</style>
